    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Greedy</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Greedy</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Make the best-looking choice now, never undo it, and still end with the best answer. This page shows when that is safe (an exchange argument), the six greedy shapes that interviews reuse (reachability, sort-and-assign, interval ends, two passes, balance counters, comparator order), and one tested template per shape in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> sorting with a custom comparator and Big-O. Greedy often hides inside other patterns: interval problems, heaps (task scheduling) and monotonic stacks (remove k digits) all make a greedy choice per step.</p>\n"
  },
